#: ../../reference/directives.md:57
msgid "Scoped Begin / End"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:59
msgid ""
"The `lang-check-begin` / `lang-check-end` directives define scoped regions "
"with richer options than basic disable/enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:68
msgid "An unclosed `lang-check-begin` extends to the end of the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:70
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:72
msgid "Options are space-separated tokens after `lang-check-begin`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:74
msgid "Rule IDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:76
msgid ""
"Bare tokens (not matching any option prefix) are treated as rule IDs. Only "
"those rules are suppressed within the region:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:85
msgid ""
"With no rule IDs and no language override, all diagnostics in the region are "
"suppressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:88
msgid "Language Override (`lang:xx`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:90
msgid ""
"Check the region in another natural language. Every prose range that starts "
"inside it is checked in that language; the rest of the document keeps "
"`engines.spell_language`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:100
msgid ""
"A region with **only** a `lang:` option (no rule IDs) is a pure language "
"override — it suppresses nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:103
msgid ""
"Regions nest, and the innermost one wins. A `lang:` directive also beats "
"whatever the markup itself declares, which is how one quoted passage inside "
"a `#set text(lang: \"de\")` document gets checked in another language "
"without touching the typesetting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:108
msgid ""
"A tag with no region is resolved before it reaches the engines. It takes the "
"document default's region when the language agrees — `lang:en` under an `en-"
"GB` document means `en-GB` — and a known variant otherwise. This matters: "
"LanguageTool accepts bare `en` and `de` and then reports no spelling errors "
"at all in them, so an unresolved tag silently checks nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:114
msgid ""
"An engine that cannot read the language says so rather than passing the "
"text. LanguageTool has no Hebrew, so a `lang:he` region produces a "
"`languagecheck.no-provider` diagnostic naming the language, and the "
"LanguageTool engine is *not* marked unhealthy for declining it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:119
msgid "Line Slice (`check[a:b]`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:121
msgid ""
"Auto-close the region using slice notation. No `lang-check-end` is needed. "
"`a` and `b` are 0-indexed line offsets after the directive (like Python "
"slicing):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:133
msgid ""
"`check[:5]` covers lines 0–4 (the first 5 lines). You can also start from an "
"offset — `check[2:5]` would cover only lines 2–4:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:136
msgid "Match Filter (`match:/PATTERN/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:138
msgid "Only apply the directive to lines matching the given regex:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:147
msgid "Exclude Filter (`exclude:/PATTERN/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:149
msgid ""
"Skip lines matching the given regex — the directive does not apply to them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:158
msgid "Type Override (`type:FORMAT`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:160
msgid ""
"Re-parse the region using a different tree-sitter grammar. The content "
"inside the region is extracted as if it were a standalone document of the "
"specified format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:170
msgid ""
"The format must be a supported language ID (e.g. `latex`, `html`, `rst`, "
"`org`). Unknown formats are skipped with a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:173
msgid "Combining Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:175
msgid "Multiple options can be combined in a single directive:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:184
msgid "Nesting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:186
msgid ""
"Begin/end regions can be nested. The inner `lang-check-end` closes the most "
"recent `lang-check-begin` (stack semantics):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:199
msgid "Scope markers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:201
msgid ""
"A bare `lang:` marker on its own line switches the language from there until "
"the next marker, with no closing directive:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:216
msgid ""
"The comment syntax follows the file: `<!-- lang: fr -->`, `// @lang: fr`, `/"
"* @lang: fr */`, `% @lang: fr`. Prose before the first marker keeps "
"`engines.spell_language`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:220
msgid ""
"Where both apply to the same position, `lang-check-begin lang:xx` wins — it "
"names a region, the marker only names a point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:223
msgid "Languages the markup declares itself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:225
msgid ""
"Some formats already carry the information, and it is read directly — no "
"directive needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md
msgid "Declaration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md
msgid "Typst"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md
msgid ""
"`#set text(lang: \"fr\", region: \"CH\")` for the rest of the enclosing "
"block, and `#text(lang: \"en\")[…]` for that content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:232
msgid ""
"Typst's `region:` becomes the BCP-47 subtag, so `lang: \"de\", region: "
"\"CH\"` is checked as `de-CH`. Only `text` is read; `lang` means something "
"else on other functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/directives.md:236
msgid ""
"A directive beats the markup, so a document can keep its typesetting "
"language and still have one passage checked in another."
msgstr ""
